> Preserve the original banana pools and shared field architecture

The source uses procedural standard-Gaussian pairs u,v mapped to x0=u,
x1=v+.5(u²−1), a unit-volume triangular bend. Its inverse makes analytic truth
available. The five exact points below show the bend before the original
512 fitting, 128 validation and 128 test rows. Native midpoint-MT Box-Muller
Double draws use seeds 9203,9209,9221; source observations cast to Float32.
Source IDs have offsets 0,10000,20000. All 1,024 prior draws use seed 9257.
These are the original synthetic teaching observations, without a substitute
distribution or external prepared dataset.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cnf_banana_toy.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;auto type=n::DType::Float64;
 auto u=n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{-2,-1,0,1,2},{5});auto base=n::stack({u,n::zeros({5},type)},1);
 auto points=m::BananaPoints(base,.5,type);auto target=n::from_vector(std::vector<double>{1.5,0,-.5,0,1.5},{5});
 if(!n::equal_bits(n::select(points,1,1),target)||n::max(n::abs(m::BananaLogProbability(points)-m::StandardNormalLogProbability(base))).item()>1e-14)throw std::runtime_error("Analytic banana");
 auto axis=n::arange(0,129,1,type)/32.-2.;auto curve=m::BananaPoints(n::stack({axis,n::zeros({129},type)},1),.5,type);
 dm::graphics::RPlot::create().lines(axis.to_vector<double>(),n::select(curve,1,1).to_vector<double>(),"v=0 banana curve",{37,99,235})
 .points(u.to_vector<double>(),std::vector<double>(5,0),"Base v=0",{100,116,139},5)
 .points(u.to_vector<double>(),target.to_vector<double>(),"Five native points",{220,38,38},4)
 .y_limits(-.7,2.6).x_label("u = x0").y_label("x1 = v + .5(u^2 - 1)")
 .title("Unit-volume bending gives an analytic teaching density").save_svg("build/cnf_banana_toy.svg");
 std::print("Five exact banana coordinates; native analytic log densities match their inverse standard-normal coordinates.\n");
}
```
// result_begin: markdown
Five exact banana coordinates; native analytic log densities match their inverse standard-normal coordinates.
\image(figures/cnf_banana_toy.svg)
// result_end

\caption(Five exact banana coordinates illustrate the original unit-volume observation generator.)
\alttext(A parabola bends five zero-height Gaussian points into the analytic banana slice.)

The fitted field is f=.3*(tanh([x,t]W1+b1)W2+b2), with W1[3,8], b1[8],
W2[8,2], b2[2]. This is **50 stored values in four leaves**. Hidden/output
kernels are initialized first with normal deviations .3/.1, then biases .05/0.
The separate log_scale[2] gives **52 values in five leaves**. Source seed 10003
warms field kernels first and global scale last. The optional reference initial
arrays are absent, so native initialization is used.

One field is reused at every RK4 evaluation. The executed graph groups the
first and second four-step halves: each depends on the **same 50 field values**,
with two additional global-scale values. The unique total is 52, not 102.
The generic original metrics retain hidden=16 and coupling_layers=4; those are
legacy harness metadata. The actual hidden width is 8, and four diagnostics
refer to quarter trajectories, not four separately parameterized field networks.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cnf_network.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main(){
 namespace n=dm::nn;n::ParameterStore p(10003);
 n::Module model([&](const n::Tensor& x){auto o=n::models::CnfDensity(p,x);
  n::model_stage("Shared field: first 4 RK4 steps",x,o.stage1);
  n::model_stage("Same field: next 4 RK4 steps",o.stage1,o.unscaled);
  return n::model_stage("Positive diagonal scale",o.unscaled,o.latent);
 },"CNF: 52 unique values / 5 leaves");
 n::ModelPlotOptions options;options.detail=n::ModelPlotDetail::Blocks;options.sizing.minimum_extent=2;options.sizing.max_planes=2;
 auto figure=model.plot(n::zeros({1,2}),options);
 if(figure.parameter_count()!=52||p.size()!=5)throw std::runtime_error("Executed CNF census");
 figure.save_svg("build/cnf_network.svg");
}
