> Inspect the original density grid and every inverse sample

The two heatmaps retain all 16,384 analytic-truth cells and all 16,384 source
model cells on their original half-cell grid, with common PDF limits [0,.20],
32 colours and physical axis orientation. This is a numerical density display,
not a global normalization integral. The fitted contours remain much less bent
than the analytic banana. Both observation and latent scatter plots retain all
1,024 supplied prior rows or inverse samples and all 128 held-out rows, on equal
physical coordinate scales. Sampling uses only the Gaussian bank and frozen
final parameters.

