> Compare integrated traces with actual discrete-map determinants

The paired panels retain both values for all 128 forward test inputs and all
1,024 supplied inverse prior inputs. The inverse determinant comes from its
own reverse-RK4 path. Forward integrated logdet varies from −.178570285 to
−.103130668; it is not just a global scalar. Actual discrete Jacobians have
positive determinants on all these retained inputs. The signed residual plot
includes every forward and inverse difference, including the largest negative
inverse error; bounds retain every row. These are numerical-error checks for
this fitted field and step count, not a general invertibility guarantee for
arbitrary stiff discrete RK4 configurations.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cnf_volume.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
