> Retain the numerical change-of-variables residual

For every supplied z the diagnostic is
numerical_log_p(inverse_RK4(z))+reverse_integrated_logdet−log phi(z).
An exact continuous flow would make this zero; finite forward/reverse RK4 and
Float32 calculations leave residuals. The source also uses a Float32-rounded
log(2pi) in its model likelihood, while the final identity reference is computed
in Double. Every residual and both coordinate roundtrips are retained below.
This per-sample identity check is not an independent density integral.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/cnf_normalization.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
