> Interpret the checks at their actual scope

The original 21 archives / 163,073 values and 144 update captures / 5,040 values
are reproduced exactly, including field Jacobians, all cumulative quarter
traces, every optimizer write, batch/history TSV, protocol and non-timing metric.
Independent NumPy calculations use manual field/RK4 pullbacks and analytic
matrix composition, with all 52 fitting coordinates, all 52 inverse coordinates,
200 field parameter-mode coordinates and all saved samples checked. They call
no native helper, external autodiff or refit and use no substitute data.

The continuous model motivates the trace integral, while finite RK4 defines
the actually computed map. The report keeps those roles distinct, exposes the
source Float32 time/coefficient policy and its refinement floor, and reserves
likelihood interpretation for exact/paired trace modes. The experiment remains
one short, fixed-seed two-dimensional fit, with a tiny full-Gaussian gain and a
diagonal-Gaussian shortfall. No adaptive solver, continuous-adjoint, exact
finite-map density, seed search, test-selected checkpoint or broad generative
benchmark claim is introduced.

